:commit:888fcadf3564b60bd485b6b74af2a8da5b92dcc9 a prov:Activity, c4h:Commit ;
    rdfs:label "Add C4 model plugin: exploration, deck and architecture explorer skills" ;
    prov:endedAtTime "2026-11-19T11:57:25Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    prov:wasAssociatedWith :agent:caviri ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/caviri/c4-model-agentic-plugin/commit/888fcadf3564b60bd485b6b74af2a8da5b92dcc9> ;
    c4h:sha "888fcadf3564b60bd485b6b74af2a8da5b92dcc9" ;
    c4h:parentSha "3c3bfe2a359a0cf59f87b007fb765f13764c3c25" ;
    c4h:message "Add C4 model plugin: exploration, deck and architecture explorer skills\n\nThree skills and one command that explore a codebase and generate a\nreveal.js explainer deck and an interactive C4 architecture explorer\nwith JSON-LD and .rete export. Includes a theoretical image annotation\nproject as a test fixture, with the output generated for it, and\nREADME screenshots taken from that output." ;
    c4h:authoredAtTime "2026-11-19T11:57:25Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    c4h:author :agent:caviri ;
    c4h:committer :agent:caviri .
:commit:1e415ac8413eb9e53fd1e596e04e3bb446097b15 a prov:Activity, c4h:Commit ;
    rdfs:label "Ontology: publish the C4 architecture ontology, Turtle export, lossless RDF round trip" ;
    prov:endedAtTime "2026-11-19T15:43:27Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    prov:wasAssociatedWith :agent:caviri ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/caviri/c4-model-agentic-plugin/commit/1e415ac8413eb9e53fd1e596e04e3bb446097b15> ;
    c4h:sha "1e415ac8413eb9e53fd1e596e04e3bb446097b15" ;
    c4h:parentSha "d89f0dd037251d898e72d4a8055810f8050aa1cd" ;
    c4h:message "Ontology: publish the C4 architecture ontology, Turtle export, lossless RDF round trip\n\nAdd ontology/ with c4.ttl (the architecture: people, systems, containers,\ndata stores, components, code, relationships, scenarios and steps,\nstates and transitions, use cases), c4-view.ttl (how the explorer draws\nit), c4-shapes.ttl (SHACL every exported graph meets), alignments.ttl,\na README, EXTENDING.md with good practices, and a worked deployment\nextension. The namespace moves from urn:arch-explorer:vocab# to\nhttps://caviri.github.io/c4-model-agentic-plugin/ontology/c4#.\n\nThe graph is now a complete description of every explorer diagram:\npositions, view defaults, legend and level names are exported, and\narchRdf.fromTriples rebuilds the model from N-Triples, Turtle or\nJSON-LD. build-explorer.mjs can build a page from a graph alone, and\ncheck-roundtrip.mjs proves the page and screenshots are identical.\n\nScenarios gain use-case fields (actor, goal, trigger, preconditions,\noutcome), filled for two example scenarios from the code. Turtle is\noffered in the export menu, the editor and every build. A model can\ncarry its own extension terms through an rdf hook. The docs site gains\nan Ontology section with generated term pages and serves the .ttl files." ;
    c4h:authoredAtTime "2026-11-19T15:43:27Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    c4h:author :agent:caviri ;
    c4h:committer :agent:caviri .
:commit:24b46bd4c76756e902fce43b04bb82f1e0488135 a prov:Activity, c4h:Commit ;
    rdfs:label "Explorer: images on elements, colours per flow, compare roll-up, editor sidebar" ;
    prov:endedAtTime "2026-11-19T19:18:38Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    prov:wasAssociatedWith :agent:caviri ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/caviri/c4-model-agentic-plugin/commit/24b46bd4c76756e902fce43b04bb82f1e0488135> ;
    c4h:sha "24b46bd4c76756e902fce43b04bb82f1e0488135" ;
    c4h:parentSha "81ad19031f64c5a5d7436a61911881f158c6ca8f" ;
    c4h:message "Explorer: images on elements, colours per flow, compare roll-up, editor sidebar\n\nImages: nodes, arrows, scenarios and steps can carry images\n(screenshots, diagrams, photos, illustrations) with required alt text,\ncaption, credit and an illustrative flag. Boxes show a badge, the panel\na gallery, and a viewer opens them full size. Builds copy relative\nimages next to the page or embed them with --embed-images; the MCP\nview draws only embedded ones and links the rest through the host.\nImages are schema:ImageObject resources in the graph and round-trip.\nThe example gets three hand-made wireframes, labelled as illustrative\nbecause the project was never run.\n\nFlows: every scenario has a colour (set, or assigned from three new\ntones per theme). The Dynamic view draws a flow in its colour, and a\nflows overlay paints the arrows each flow travels on the map, with\nnumbered chips and a legend; shared arrows show stripes. show_flows is\na new page and MCP tool.\n\nCompare mode tints added, removed and changed parts on the map in the\nsame colours as the change list, and rolls changes up: a closed box\nshows +N -N ~N for everything inside it, merged arrows carry their\nchanges, and selecting a box lists the changes inside it.\n\nEditor: edit mode gets a sidebar in place of the details panel, with\nan Add palette grouped by C4 level to drag onto the map or into the\noutline, an outline tree to filter, re-parent and reorder by drag,\nand grouped properties including images and the flow colour. Every\naction is undoable and works by mouse, touch and keyboard." ;
    c4h:authoredAtTime "2026-11-19T19:18:38Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    c4h:author :agent:caviri ;
    c4h:committer :agent:caviri .
